[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-90-docs-business-cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.md", :doc/title "cloud-itonami — vertical maturity (design vs implementation)", :doc/path "90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn", :doc/body "# cloud-itonami — vertical maturity (design vs implementation)\n\n**As-of**: 2026-07-22  \n**Product**: `cloud-itonami`  \n**正本 (structured)**: `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`  \n**Portfolio scores**: `maturity-facts.edn` + generated `maturity-scores.md` (ADR-2607021700)  \n**Flagship sprint**: ADR-2607122300  \n\nThis is the *within-product* breakdown. Portfolio BMC/YC answers “is the\nbusiness mature?”; this doc answers “where inside the fleet is that maturity?”\n\n## Rubric (0–5)\n\n| Axis | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Design** | Domain scope, Governor discipline, op contract, ADR/blueprint clarity |\n| **Impl-core** | `operation` / governor|policy / `store` / `phase` / `sim` / `facts` present and tested |\n| **Impl-product** | Live demo, operator-quickstart, CI regen, pricing docs |\n| **Business** | External tenant, billing, hyp validation |\n\n## Fleet snapshot (mechanical)\n\nLocal ISIC checkouts under `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-*` (**n=165**):\n\n| module-score (0–6) | count | reading |\n|---|---:|---|\n| 6 | **127** | full actor modules |\n| 5 | 3 | near-full |\n| 0 | **35** | thin / empty src |\n\n| product-score (0–5) | count | reading |\n|---|---:|---|\n| 5 | **2** | 6399, 6310 only |\n| 4 | **1** | 7810 |\n| 3 | 16 | mostly mfg demos / sample HTML |\n| 1–2 | **146** | actor without storefront |\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry (updated **2026-07-14T19:00:00Z**):\n\n| maturity | count |\n|---|---:|\n| `:implemented` | **286** |\n| `:blueprint` | 1 |\n| `:spec` | **345** |\n\n## Cohort table\n\n| Vertical / layer | Design | Impl-core | Impl-product | Business | One-liner |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| **6399 Meta job-search** | 5 | 5 | 5 | **2** | Indeed replacement; 6 jurisdictions; live demo; aozora.app actor + first promo post (ADR-2607161930); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Starter tier (ADR-2607161745), no paid org yet |\n| **6310 Talent** | 5 | 5 | 5 | **2** | kaonavi replacement; assignment op; live demo; aozora.app actor + first promo post (ADR-2607161930); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Starter tier (ADR-2607161745), no paid org yet |\n| **7810 Employment/placement** | 4 | 4 | 4 | **2** | Near-flagship (demo + quickstart); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Starter tier (ADR-2607161745), no paid org yet |\n| **Insurance / finance** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Full modules; almost no storefront |\n| **Real estate** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Same pattern |\n| **Health / care / hospital** | 5 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Strong clinical scope exclusion; thin product face |\n| **Education (855/8510/8521/8522/8530/8541/8542/8549/8550/8569, 10 repos)** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Full modules; no product face. 851/852/853/854 split out 2026-07-22/23 into their own flagship rows below (ADR-2607220200 + follow-up /loop iterations). 855 gained DatomicStore store-parity and 3 real governor/store bug fixes (safety-flag phase-gating, escalation-reason preservation, unreachable session-registration branch -- 23/23 tests) but has no pricing docs or billing yet, so it stays in this shared row. The 9 four-digit repos (8510-8569) were spot-checked and found already healthy (0 test failures, 0 lint issues each) -- clean bill of health, no fixes needed. Promoting any of these 10 (pricing docs, billing) is a separate decision this ADR does not make.\n| **852 Secondary Education (flagship)** | 4 | 4 | 4 | **2** | Governed secondary-school administrative-coordination actor (attendance/scheduling/supply/staffing/safety-flag proposals; permanent scope-exclusion on grading/curriculum/discipline/custody); `secondaryops.store` gained `DatomicStore` parity (43 tests/146 assertions, 0 failures); reuses isic-851's K-12 pricing-intel 20260722-01 research (same market, different grade band; deliberately NOT the ¥50k-150k/月 portfolio-uniform range); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed School Ops (Starter) ¥25,000/月, no paid org yet. **Correction (2026-07-24): the initial 2026-07-23 flagship promotion was premature** -- it closed pricing docs + billing (items 5/7) but never verified items 2/4/6 (build-time demo + nightly workflow + registry :demo field), and business-model.md's Funnel section wrongly claimed a demo generator existed. Now actually built: `secondaryops.render-html` (ported from isic-851's identical actor shape, verified idempotent), `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml` (confirmed via a live `workflow_dispatch` run, conclusion=success), and the registry `:demo` field (confirmed HTTP 200, serving the real generated content). This vertical is now genuinely flagship-complete.\n| **853 Higher Education (flagship)** | 4 | 4 | 4 | **2** | Governed higher-education advising/facility/staffing-coordination actor; `highereds.store` gained `DatomicStore` parity (42 tests/140 assertions, 0 failures); pricing-intel 20260723-01, fresh research for this genuinely different market (WaitWell $29/mo, SuperSaaS $9/mo, Slate $30k/year cited only as the ceiling; ¥8k-25k/月 band, deliberately NOT the ¥50k-150k/月 portfolio-uniform range); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Advising Ops (Starter) ¥20,000/月, no paid org yet. Same 2026-07-24 completion as 852, but building the demo here first required closing a REAL architecture gap: `highereds.governor/govern` only decided (:hold/:commit/:escalate) -- nothing wired that decision to a store mutation or ledger fact, so a faithful demo was impossible without it. Added `highereds.operation/execute-proposal!` + `approve-and-commit!` (49 tests/165 assertions, up from 42/140) and fixed the SAME `:flag-safety-concern` phase-gating bug isic-855 had (excluded from phase-1/phase-2 entirely, contradicting the governor's own always-escalate logic and the file's own doc comments) -- 2 existing tests that encoded the bug were updated. `highereds.render-html`, `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml` (live run confirmed success), and the registry `:demo` field are all now real and verified.\n| **854 Vocational/Continuing Education (flagship)** | 4 | 4 | 4 | **2** | Governed adult vocational/continuing-education coordination actor; deps.edn's `:test` alias was completely non-functional (0 of 18 tests could run) and had no langgraph/langchain dependency at all, unlike every sibling -- fixed to the fleet-standard shape AND given `DatomicStore` parity in the same pass (22 tests/60 assertions, 0 failures, was: 0 runnable); pricing-intel 20260723-01 anchored against the nearest real comparables (TalentLMS/Trainual/Coursebox, an admittedly imperfect LMS-category match honestly documented as such; ¥12k-30k/月 band); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed Training Ops (Starter) ¥20,000/月, no paid org yet. Same 2026-07-24 completion, same missing-dispatcher gap as 853: added `vocationalops.operation/execute-proposal!` + `approve-and-commit!` (30 tests/85 assertions, up from 29/84). Actually running the real pipeline (not just isolated unit tests) surfaced a genuine bug no prior test caught: `advisor/propose-supply-request`'s own rationale said \\\"non-instructional consumables\\\" -- but \\\"instructional\\\" is one of governor's scope-excluded-terms, so the advisor's own correct description of this in-scope op false-triggered a HARD scope-exclusion hold on every single proposal of this type. Fixed with a docs/description-only wording change (governor's security-critical term list itself was untouched, to avoid weakening a HARD check) + a regression test. `vocationalops.render-html`, `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml` (live run confirmed success), and the registry `:demo` field are all now real and verified.\n| **851 Primary Education (flagship)** | 4 | 4 | 4 | **2** | Governed primary/pre-primary school administrative-coordination actor (attendance/scheduling/supply/staffing/safety-flag proposals; permanent scope-exclusion on grading/curriculum/discipline/custody); `schoolops.store` gained `DatomicStore` parity with the rest of the flagship cohort (43 tests/146 assertions, 0 failures); pricing-intel 20260722-01 (\u00a515k\u2013\u00a540k/\u6708 band, deliberately NOT the \u00a550k-150k/\u6708 portfolio-uniform range -- no evidenced relationship to K-12 school pricing); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed School Ops (Starter) \u00a525,000/\u6708 (ADR-2607220200), no paid org yet. |\n| **Mfg / auto** | 4 | 4 | 3 | 0 | Higher demo-HTML rate; no operator funnel |\n| **2910 Motor-vehicle manufacture (next-up candidate)** | 4 | 4 | 3 | 0 | ISIC Rev.5 2910; full module set (operation/governor/store/phase/sim/facts) + robotics wired to a real physics/scene engine (ADR-2607151600). 2026-07-18 wave5 iteration 4: added `automotive.render-html` + `.github/workflows/regenerate.yml` -- `docs/samples/operator-console.html` (the file actually self-labeled 'Demo snapshot ... clojure -M:dev:run', NOT `docs/index.html` as ledger seq 3 misstated) is now build-time-generated through the real actor; verified idempotent locally, against a from-scratch CI-layout simulation, and via a live `workflow_dispatch` run (conclusion=success, https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2910/actions/runs/29649931361, its own 'commit when changed' step logging 'console unchanged' confirming the byte-identical idempotent regeneration), and confirmed the live Pages URL now serves the generated content. Iteration 4 also found ledger seq 3's 'no operator-quickstart.md, no pricing/billing docs found' claim was incorrect -- both `docs/operator-quickstart.md` (52 lines) and `docs/business-model.md` (38 lines) already existed pre-iteration-4; `business-model.md` has qualitative revenue categories but no quantified pricing or Stripe link yet (checklist items 5/7 remain open). `docs/index.html` itself remains a static marketing page (not build-time-generated, but also not mislabeled as live data -- its own footer already says 'no invented usage or revenue metrics'). Still NOT promoted to the flagship cohort -- promotion is a separate decision this iteration did not make. |\n| **Infra / utility** | 4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | Some thinner checkouts |\n| **5820 CRM (Salesforce replace)** | 5 | 4 | 4 | **2** | RevOps-LLM ⊣ SubscriptionGovernor; live face /isic-5820/; kotoba-lang/crm west-registered (ADR-2607172500); pricing-intel 20260717-01 (¥50k–150k band); Stripe Payment Link live for Managed CRM Starter ¥80k/月 (ADR-2607172600), no paid org yet. ⚠ 2026-07-18 gap audit (ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 3): flagship checklist item 2 (build-time-generated demo) is NOT met -- docs/index.html was hand-authored in a single commit (cbbe532 'Lane C densify'), contains generic unfilled placeholders ('maturity unknown', literal `governor` name) and a broken CTA link to the wrong repo (isco-1212, not 5820); no generate.cljs/web/ build script exists anywhere in the repo history. Axis scores above are NOT re-verified against this finding -- flagged for human review, not auto-demoted per rollout guardrail. |\n| **Software/IT 620x** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | 6201/6202/6209 CRM-fleet siblings sharing kotoba-lang/crm commons; thin product face |\n| **ISO3166 countries** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | Country coordinators; no GTM surface |\n| **ISO3166 JPN agencies** | 4 | 0 | 1 | 0 | blueprint + docs; essentially no src |\n| **ISCO occupations** | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 | open-occupation 88/88 :implemented (PR #427); product face still thin |\n| **Catalog / org surface** | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | github.io from registry SSoT |\n| **itonami.cloud cockpit** | 4 | 4 | 5 | 2 | free-path productSurface 5716/5716; free tenants=4; agentRuns7d~22k; Stripe readyForLiveCheckout (live); hyp/itonami-smb-pay measuring; no paid org yet |\n\n## Reading\n\n```\nDesign        ████████████████████  high across the factory\nImpl-core     ████████████████░░░░  ~77% of local ISIC full modules\nImpl-product  ██████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  cockpit + flagships; thin elsewhere\nBusiness      ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  free-tenant ok; paid hyp untested\n```\n\n**Design maturity and implementation maturity are not uncorrelated —\nimplementation has split into core vs product.** Core was mass-produced;\nproduct was invested in flagships + the itonami.cloud cockpit (now\nproductSurface 7/7); business has not cleared a paid gate on any vertical.\n\n## Priorities (from this table)\n\n1. ~~Owner STRIPE_*** secrets → live `/isco-1212` checkout~~ — **done\n   2026-07-16 (ADR-2607161620)**: secrets wired to Cloudflare Pages, live\n   Stripe Product/2 metered Price/Webhook created. Remaining gate is now\n   **E2E checkout verification (skipped, still open) → first paid org**.\n2. Prefer **product → business** on 6399 / 6310 (+7810) over new verticals. **5820 (Salesforce-replace CRM) joined this flagship cohort 2026-07-17** (owner directive; ADR-2607172600). 2026-07-18 audit found 5820's demo page is hand-authored, not build-time-generated (checklist item 2 gap, see cohort-table note; ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 3) -- still open, out of scope for a single bounded iteration (5820's actor shape has no HTML-render entrypoint at all). **isic-2910 (motor-vehicle manufacture) registered 2026-07-18 as the next-up new-vertical candidate** (same ADR, ledger seq 3); **its matching build-time-generation gap was closed 2026-07-18 wave5 iteration 4** (ledger seq 4, see cohort-table note) -- still not promoted to the flagship cohort. **cloud-itonami-isic-851 (Primary Education) joined this flagship cohort 2026-07-22** (owner directive; ADR-2607220200) -- the first flagship promotion scoped explicitly to the PROVEN pattern (store parity + pricing docs + Stripe link) rather than a novel bespoke API/claim-page buildout; its pricing band deliberately deviates from the portfolio-uniform \u00a550k-150k/\u6708 range because real K-12 school-admin competitor research does not support that range.\n3. Keep the portfolio wedge narrative on the flagship pair (`:wedge 3` in\n   maturity-facts; not “all industries” as the sales wedge).\n4. Treat ISO3166 agencies and ISCO as **design assets**; defer runtime spend.\n5. Portfolio `validation` / `revenue` stay 0 until\n   `:hyp/itonami-smb-pay` (10 external paid orgs).\n6. **2026-07-18 wave5 iteration 5**: built a read-only fleet-wide diagnostic scanner\n   (`90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-checklist-scan.cljs`) instead of continuing\n   one-repo-at-a-time hand-diagnosis, and ran it over all 1,109 real local\n   `orgs/cloud-itonami-*` checkouts (1,116 dirs found, 7 without `.git`). Validated\n   against the 5 known-ground-truth repos before trusting it (isic-6399 correctly\n   scored fully clean; isic-5820 correctly scored no-generator; isic-6310/7810/2910\n   correctly flagged `checkout-lag=true`, explaining why their on-disk state still\n   looks unfixed even though iterations 1/2/4 already fixed them on GitHub — see\n   ledger seq 5 for the root cause, a `manifest/west.yml` pin-staleness bug this\n   iteration also fixed). **Strategic finding, reported instead of forcing a token\n   fix**: zero *new* \"cheap win\" repos exist (a repo with an existing generator\n   script but a missing nightly workflow) — the only 3 repos with any generator\n   script at all are the 3 already known. 930/1,109 (84%) of the fleet has **no\n   demo file whatsoever** (not even a hand-authored one); another 176/1,109 (16%)\n   have a hand-authored demo but no generator. The iteration-1/2 \"port the\n   isic-6399 regenerate.yml template\" playbook has run out of targets — closing\n   checklist item 2 on any new repo now requires a bespoke build-time renderer\n   written from that repo's own actor shape (the isic-2910 pattern, ledger seq 4),\n   roughly one iteration of work per repo, not a template port.\n7. **2026-07-19 wave5 iteration 6**: tested whether a REUSABLE generator template\n   could beat the \"one bespoke renderer per repo\" marginal cost iteration 5\n   projected. Sampled 13 no-demo repos across unrelated ISIC sectors: 11/13\n   shared the isic-2910 actor shape (`src/<domain>/{facts,phase,sim,governor,\n   operation,advisor,store}.cljc` + root `deps.edn`, no `web/`, no `http.clj`);\n   a full filesystem pass over all 1,109 real checkouts confirmed **290/1,109\n   (26% of the fleet)** additionally share an IDENTICAL real `langgraph.graph`\n   StateGraph shape (same node names, same channels, same\n   `:interrupt-before #{:request-approval}`, spot-checked across 8 repos with\n   zero divergence) -- large and homogeneous enough to justify a template, but\n   NOT a majority of the full fleet (33% match the coarser shape signature;\n   ~26% are still pre-actor stubs; ~41% are structurally different). Built a\n   copy-and-adapt template (not a shared library dependency -- this fleet's\n   repos are deliberately standalone/forkable) with 4 explicit adaptation\n   points, and proved it end-to-end on 2 repos from the sample:\n   **cloud-itonami-isic-851** (schoolops) and **cloud-itonami-isic-6820**\n   (realty) -- both verified locally (real actor output, idempotent reruns),\n   byte-identical under a from-scratch CI-layout simulation, merged, and\n   confirmed via a live `workflow_dispatch` run to `conclusion=success` +\n   live GitHub Pages URL serving the new content. Also caught a real,\n   pre-existing latent bug while mining isic-851's own `schoolops.sim` demo\n   driver for scenario data: it used ids copy-pasted from an unrelated\n   eldercare actor that don't exist in schoolops' own seeded data, so every\n   one of its calls actually HARD-held regardless of the \"happy path\" its own\n   comments claimed -- did not reuse it uncritically, wrote a corrected\n   scenario against the real seed data instead. Fleet-wide checklist item 2\n   count: 3 -> 5 generated, 930 -> 928 no-demo. Template + full evidence:\n   `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-generator-template.edn`.\n\n8. **2026-07-22/23 `/loop` coverage sweep**: after fixing isic-854/855's genuinely broken test runners (0 runnable tests each, silently invisible until someone actually tried `clojure -M:test`), sampled 17 OTHER checked-out repos for the same class of issue -- all 9 remaining ISIC-85 four-digit repos (8510/8521/8522/8530/8541/8542/8549/8550/8569) plus 8 diverse non-education repos spanning manufacturing (2599, 3311), wholesale trade (4610), hospitality (5610), real estate (6820), healthcare (8610), personal services (9601), and insurance (6511). Clean bill of health across all 17: every one passes `clojure -M:dev:test` with 0 failures/0 errors and `clojure -M:lint` with 0 errors/0 warnings. Conclusion: isic-854/855's breakage was isolated to those two repos (both show genuine structural divergence from the fleet-standard actor shape), not a fleet-wide systemic pattern. A future session doesn't need to redo this exact 17-repo sample looking for the same issue; if a broader sweep is wanted, it should target repos NOT yet touched by any verification pass rather than re-sampling ones already confirmed healthy.\n\n9. **2026-07-24 fleet-sample round 2**: extended the round-1 17-repo sample with 15 MORE repos from clusters not yet touched -- food/beverage manufacturing (1071 bakery, 1101 distilling), rubber/metal/instrument manufacturing (2211 tyre, 2591 metal forming, 3220 musical instruments), auto repair (4520), pharmacy retail (4772), hospitality (5510), wireless telecom (6120), management consulting (7020), advertising (7310), veterinary (7500), private security (8010), sports events (9319), appliance repair (9522). Clean bill of health across all 15 (24-88 tests / 103-250 assertions each, 0 failures/0 errors, clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings). Cumulative fleet-sample total: 32/32 repos healthy outside the isic-854/855 incident, which itself is now fully fixed. Reinforces round 1's conclusion that 854/855 were isolated, not a fleet-wide pattern -- no further broad sampling is planned unless a specific new signal (e.g. another repo reported as broken) warrants it.\n\n## Related\n\n- Portfolio rescore note: `maturity-facts.edn` `:cloud-itonami` (2026-07-16)\n- Stripe billing go-live: ADR-2607161620\n- 6399/6310 aozora.app distribution actors: ADR-2607161930\n- 6399/6310/7810 flagship Managed-tier Stripe Payment Links + pricing-intelligence: ADR-2607161745\n- 5820 Salesforce-replace flagship promotion: ADR-2607172600\n- 851 Primary Education flagship-parity promotion (DatomicStore + pricing-intel 20260722-01 + Managed School Ops Starter Stripe link): ADR-2607220200 (2026-07-22)\n- 5820 demo-generation gap audit + 2910 next-up candidate registration: ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 3 (2026-07-18)\n- 2910 build-time-demo-generation gap closed (automotive.render-html + regenerate.yml): ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 4 (2026-07-18)\n- Fleet-wide read-only diagnostic scanner + report: `90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-checklist-scan.cljs` / `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-checklist-scan.edn` (generated), west.yml pin-staleness fix (commit f2c635cc): ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 5 (2026-07-18)\n- Reusable generator template (290/1,109-repo cluster) + isic-851/isic-6820 proof: `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-generator-template.edn`, ADR-2607189300 ledger seq 6 (2026-07-19)\n- Metrics: `metrics/cloud-itonami.edn` (cockpit traffic)\n- Flagship depth: ADR-2607122300\n- Pattern saturation (earlier): ADR-2607011200", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/doc_type "doc"}]